  "adaptation": "Header original Hero/Section page, scroll-width Motion navbar, real mobile drawer/overlay/open-close, local ThemeToggle. Original navLinks all / and page has no matching anchors: navigation/active-section success is NOT claimed. Free-trial links are disconnected. Button aria-labels added only for menu open/close; source geometry and variants retained. Original full Eldora page and local component tree retained, with narrow documented framework adaptations. Next Link is a local inert anchor with visible disabled-destination title; all default anchor navigation prevented, no successful routing or checkout is simulated. Original button/CVA/Radix source retained. Only required original Icons.logo wrapper/Logo and cn retained, unrelated icon/site helpers omitted. NextThemes replaced by local in-memory context preserving theme on hidden/remount, no storage/OS setting access. Original globals.css, Tailwind4 and tw-animate-css compiled; native system font rather than downloaded Geist. Host adds scope note, error handling, hidden subtree unmount/restore, owned listener/RAF/WAAPI/timeouts cleanup, atlas:dispose/pagehide; animation records finish/cancel removal retains original onfinish. Hidden cancels owned timers, including original500ms manual-scroll flag timer. No network, clipboard, backend or binary assets. Original brand/sample marketing text is demo material, not endorsement or an offer. Test uses controlled RAF/performance/640px geometry, actual540compose, 100hide/reveal cycles and actual original state; not native pixel/WAAPI/layout verification. Actual emitted dependency identities are resolved to the nearest named/versioned package root, including both installed paths each of react-aria3.53.1 and react-stately3.51.0 in pricing; parsed-only outer wrappers are not mislabeled as runtime. These Apache distributions contain LICENSE but no NOTICE files. Complete exact runtime notices and CSS licenses retained.",
